#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054399 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf8a6a4f-38ce-5ece-bdcb-6f2b58e2605c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a One-Step Inequality"}] :question/id #uuid "121c55cc-404a-53e7-81f7-6edba34b0796" :question/math-academy-id "e-12956" :question/problem "What is the solution to $7z \\lt -21?$" :question/worked-solution "The variable $z$ is being *multiplied* by $7.$ To isolate $z$, we perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $7.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7z & <-21 \\\\ \\frac{7z}{7} & <\\frac{-21}{7} \\\\ \\frac{7z}{7} & <-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $7$ from the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7z}{7} & <-3 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{7}z}{\\cancel{7}} & <-3 \\\\ z & <-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z \\lt -3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054400 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054770 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "281841fb-287e-597a-abb1-3917212e0dcb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a One-Step Inequality When Flipping Is Required"}] :question/id #uuid "7424a287-2269-5044-abb7-1004b3826aca" :question/math-academy-id "e-12957" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-6x \\leq -7 .$" :question/worked-solution "The variable $x$ is being *multiplied* by $-6.$ To isolate $x,$ we perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-6.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\nAlso, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6x\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,-7 \\\\ \\frac{-6x}{-6}\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,\\frac{-7}{-6} \\\\ \\frac{-6x}{-6}\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,\\frac{7}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $-6$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-6x}{-6} & \\ge \\frac{7}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-6}x}{\\cancel{-6}} & \\ge \\frac{7}{6} \\\\ x & \\ge \\frac{7}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x \\geq \\dfrac{7}{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054401 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054771 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "200fc394-b299-5114-8f39-e6265f3c1166" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a One-Step Inequality With Fractions When Flipping Is Required"}] :question/id #uuid "82a9a75f-ab0e-54c3-9a0d-82c8497714cb" :question/math-academy-id "e-12958" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-\\dfrac{y}{8} \\leq -4.$" :question/worked-solution "The variable $y$ is being *divided* by $8.$ To isolate $y$ and remove the negative sign, we *multiply* by $-8.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{y}{8}\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,-4 \\\\ (-8)\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{8})\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,(-8)\\cdot (-4) \\\\ (-8)\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{8})\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince two negative numbers multiply to give a positive number, we first cancel the negatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-8)\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{8}) & \\ge 32 \\\\ (\\cancel{-}8)\\cdot (\\cancel{-}\\frac{y}{8}) & \\ge 32 \\\\ 8\\cdot \\frac{y}{8} & \\ge 32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $8$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\cdot \\frac{y}{8} & \\ge 32 \\\\ \\frac{8y}{8} & \\ge 32 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{8}y}{\\cancel{8}} & \\ge 32 \\\\ y & \\ge 32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y \\geq 32.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054402 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054772 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b0cad0-354b-5c4c-9fe2-3aceff7e5b6e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality and Adjusting the Final Result"}] :question/id #uuid "1154ded3-0841-5358-980c-15c0f1841e82" :question/math-academy-id "e-12959" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-9 \\leq -3z.$" :question/worked-solution "The variable $z$ is being *multiplied* by $-3.$ To isolate $z,$ we can perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-3.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\nAlso, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,-3z \\\\ \\frac{-9}{-3}\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,\\frac{-3z}{-3} \\\\ 3\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,\\frac{-3z}{-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel the common factor $-3$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & \\ge \\frac{-3z}{-3} \\\\ 3 & \\ge \\frac{\\cancel{-3}z}{\\cancel{-3}} \\\\ 3 & \\ge z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the inequality with the variable on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\nz \\leq 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z \\leq 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054772 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b0cad0-354b-5c4c-9fe2-3aceff7e5b6e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality and Adjusting the Final Result"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d49bfa7-1f01-5706-a0d7-e212b240aefa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488501} {:answer/id #uuid "2c309931-42a9-5cfe-b8c7-ab31de9c391e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488564} {:answer/id #uuid "70e73623-91bd-50c1-b2a5-5488adf5f0f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le 36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488696} {:answer/id #uuid "b31cdb4f-cbb5-581f-bd40-300852926061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488828} {:answer/id #uuid "d7aca673-1ac9-5202-859a-b0c90a3cce98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c309931-42a9-5cfe-b8c7-ab31de9c391e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488564} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b247723-10a2-59dd-a722-3e6fa2bf5abb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d0eabfed-9153-5a03-9ac2-bd2dd6f86cff" :question/math-academy-id "q-153986" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $9\\ge -\\frac{x}{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "The variable $x$ is being *divided* by $4.$ To isolate $x$ and remove the negative sign, we *multiply* by $-4$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,-\\frac{x}{4} \\\\ (-4)\\cdot 9\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,(-4)\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{4}) \\\\ -36\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,(-4)\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince two negative numbers multiply to give a positive number, we first cancel the negatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-36\\,\\, & \\le (-4)\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{4}) \\\\ -36 & \\le (\\cancel{-}4)\\cdot (\\cancel{-}\\frac{x}{4}) \\\\ -36 & \\le 4\\cdot \\frac{x}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel the common factor $4$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-36 & \\le 4\\cdot \\frac{x}{4} \\\\ -36 & \\le \\frac{4x}{4} \\\\ -36 & \\le \\frac{\\cancel{4}x}{\\cancel{4}} \\\\ -36 & \\le x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the inequality with the variable on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\nx\\ge -36\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\ge -36.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489177 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf8a6a4f-38ce-5ece-bdcb-6f2b58e2605c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a One-Step Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12d87434-71e4-54f1-a372-a90ef20ae75d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z\\le 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488510} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc8da54-086c-5d9b-9b14-53ceba53d9ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z\\ge -5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488531} {:answer/id #uuid "dee2b797-cda8-58c5-8c9e-c84cf539e038" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z\\ge 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488933} {:answer/id #uuid "f4a7b970-1d79-5d22-b73b-66e22c594805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z\\ge -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488987} {:answer/id #uuid "fea4596e-6f88-5c8f-b6b5-dbe15e1e0a49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z\\le -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4a7b970-1d79-5d22-b73b-66e22c594805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z\\ge -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488987} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5fcf5cd-756a-5156-b600-8af6deb086fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0adffdfa-69ac-5e5a-b37a-c75c3775b1c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-153991" :question/problem "What is the solution to $z-1\\ge -4?$" :question/worked-solution "To isolate $z,$ we need to perform the *opposite* of *subtracting* $1,$ which is *adding* $1.$\nRemember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-1 & \\ge -4 \\\\ z-1+1 & \\ge -4+1 \\\\ z+0 & \\ge -3 \\\\ z & \\ge -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z\\ge -3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf8a6a4f-38ce-5ece-bdcb-6f2b58e2605c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a One-Step Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51a7617f-c2a9-5b2f-afbc-fa61d75db63c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z<-\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488627} {:answer/id #uuid "873cc3bb-ee3e-5f8d-bb70-1f9622a20699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z>-\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488736} {:answer/id #uuid "e187f681-af80-55e0-b5e0-cda9b0106e4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z>-\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488939} {:answer/id #uuid "ec567112-8cbf-5700-a988-c951b4136788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z<\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488968} {:answer/id #uuid "f234b7db-2841-5fcd-9af4-04eae68cbc33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z>\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488982}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e187f681-af80-55e0-b5e0-cda9b0106e4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z>-\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488939} :answer-field/id #uuid "07997d85-964b-554b-8dcd-cbd474e99af8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a32936a3-d0e7-5359-880f-a816d9cf59f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-153998" :question/problem "What is the solution to $6z>-5?$" :question/worked-solution "The variable $z$ is being *multiplied* by $6.$ To isolate $z,$ we perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $6.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6z & >-5 \\\\ \\frac{6z}{6} & >\\frac{-5}{6} \\\\ \\frac{6z}{6} & >-\\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $6$ from the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6z}{6} & >-\\frac{5}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{6}z}{\\cancel{6}} & >-\\frac{5}{6} \\\\ z & >-\\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z>-\\frac{5}{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489281 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054770 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "281841fb-287e-597a-abb1-3917212e0dcb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a One-Step Inequality When Flipping Is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54f93c73-41c6-57b8-a8f6-00ee1584e547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488632} {:answer/id #uuid "95c1fbc3-7cd8-5d44-a9cd-13b7ff43dbe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488772} {:answer/id #uuid "c3db2312-b3f3-544b-a4f9-1ec3c358e1e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488867} {:answer/id #uuid "dc62b0bf-4eb8-5cb3-a5b3-d5feadf29eb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488927} {:answer/id #uuid "ec006aca-e22f-576f-822a-97d6e8403ccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec006aca-e22f-576f-822a-97d6e8403ccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488967} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb6518e0-b1be-56b3-b252-cbc313544571" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489121}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e481e652-2dec-5a50-9597-483a3ddecf5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-154000" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-5x<10.$" :question/worked-solution "The variable $x$ is being *multiplied* by $-5.$ To isolate $x,$ we perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-5.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\nAlso, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5x\\,\\, & <\\,\\,10 \\\\ \\frac{-5x}{-5}\\,\\, & >\\,\\,\\frac{10}{-5} \\\\ \\frac{-5x}{-5}\\,\\, & >\\,\\,-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $-5$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-5x}{-5} & >-2 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-5}x}{\\cancel{-5}} & >-2 \\\\ x & >-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x>-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489269 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054770 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "281841fb-287e-597a-abb1-3917212e0dcb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a One-Step Inequality When Flipping Is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "042fc76b-dd56-5806-addd-4531f4fef204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y<-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488478} {:answer/id #uuid "9295930a-b171-5b3e-8f56-ddb4f4b4ba94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488763} {:answer/id #uuid "a24dde04-3090-5fa2-8910-e9ca71945abc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y<6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488791} {:answer/id #uuid "ae1366b6-970c-5084-b08f-cca2225416c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488815} {:answer/id #uuid "d31a53bc-a400-50cc-81d8-db4e5161d98a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9295930a-b171-5b3e-8f56-ddb4f4b4ba94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488763} :answer-field/id #uuid "1380a716-2626-5dcb-b0e7-7da3ff3f8711" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489031}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf24a3ad-fa5d-5add-9240-16d745dab1cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-154001" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-3y<-18.$" :question/worked-solution "The variable $y$ is being *multiplied* by $-3.$ To isolate $y,$ we perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-3.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\nAlso, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3y\\,\\, & <\\,\\,-18 \\\\ \\frac{-3y}{-3}\\,\\, & >\\,\\,\\frac{-18}{-3} \\\\ \\frac{-3y}{-3}\\,\\, & >\\,\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $-3$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-3y}{-3} & >6 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-3}y}{\\cancel{-3}} & >6 \\\\ y & >6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y>6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489248 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054770 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "281841fb-287e-597a-abb1-3917212e0dcb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a One-Step Inequality When Flipping Is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b46405b-3ad9-5210-97ea-a7b2916ffbeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z>-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488495} {:answer/id #uuid "0cc5085c-c9b6-5fbb-8598-97b62491c07b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z<5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488500} {:answer/id #uuid "3587e5dc-d9f6-5563-a641-10752ed41539" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z<\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488581} {:answer/id #uuid "6e20e665-ff20-5580-9690-6db3c3be0861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z>\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488686} {:answer/id #uuid "acd2dce3-53b8-5390-83c7-26cfe4458a8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z<-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b46405b-3ad9-5210-97ea-a7b2916ffbeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z>-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488495} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca4e6dfe-98d3-5a29-8be0-91b478dc3f64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9c17e0c0-dc11-5aeb-b1ca-6cfde8f72eed" :question/math-academy-id "q-154002" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-2z<7.$" :question/worked-solution "The variable $z$ is being *multiplied* by $-2.$ To isolate $z,$ we perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-2.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\nAlso, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2z\\,\\, & <\\,\\,7 \\\\ \\frac{-2z}{-2}\\,\\, & >\\,\\,\\frac{7}{-2} \\\\ \\frac{-2z}{-2}\\,\\, & >\\,\\,-\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $-2$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-2z}{-2} & >-\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-2}z}{\\cancel{-2}} & >-\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ z & >-\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z>-\\frac{7}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489197 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054771 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "200fc394-b299-5114-8f39-e6265f3c1166" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a One-Step Inequality With Fractions When Flipping Is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27055c91-5496-54a5-a484-9ee0db9c9232" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\le -32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488551} {:answer/id #uuid "74fe5fa6-f788-5018-bdad-67fe0261dcfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\ge 32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488701} {:answer/id #uuid "a634d207-164b-5687-8998-961c7b33c805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\le 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488801} {:answer/id #uuid "b37e6a67-494b-57c7-b107-a4d9f4fb48d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\le 32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488829} {:answer/id #uuid "b4fa7825-9607-55f9-afee-7c78dcee3ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\ge -32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b37e6a67-494b-57c7-b107-a4d9f4fb48d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\le 32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488829} :answer-field/id #uuid "f17c9881-f4b3-5038-8fce-eff3a19f4f64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489157}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c5ad69f-c453-5e7c-98b1-f37e29e67532" :question/math-academy-id "q-154011" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-\\frac{y}{4}\\ge -8.$" :question/worked-solution "The variable $y$ is being *divided* by $4.$ To isolate $y$ and remove the negative sign, we *multiply* by $-4.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{y}{4}\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,-8 \\\\ (-4)\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{4})\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,(-4)\\cdot (-8) \\\\ (-4)\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{4})\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince two negative numbers multiply to give a positive number, we first cancel the negatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-4)\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{4}) & \\le 32 \\\\ (\\cancel{-}4)\\cdot (\\cancel{-}\\frac{y}{4}) & \\le 32 \\\\ 4\\cdot \\frac{y}{4} & \\le 32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $4$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot \\frac{y}{4} & \\le 32 \\\\ \\frac{4y}{4} & \\le 32 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4}y}{\\cancel{4}} & \\le 32 \\\\ y & \\le 32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y\\le 32.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489185 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054772 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b0cad0-354b-5c4c-9fe2-3aceff7e5b6e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality and Adjusting the Final Result"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c751dfa4-9a34-55a9-977b-a7ae8c48f146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c751dfa4-9a34-55a9-977b-a7ae8c48f146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488877} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a0ccd33-4c2d-58e0-b379-0e66b9afdd14" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489025} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1e75e85-1d53-5120-b20e-3a2333c53a2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1e75e85-1d53-5120-b20e-3a2333c53a2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488900} :answer-field/id #uuid "1250e176-4bda-5a9c-93d0-2dbe8c8275a1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1c83e356-5c28-5a7c-9e2e-dbd984ca824b" :question/math-academy-id "q-171618" :question/problem "The solution to the inequality $24<6y$ is $y${{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The variable $y$ is being *multiplied* by $6.$ To isolate $y,$ we perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $6.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24 & <6y \\\\ \\frac{24}{6} & <\\frac{6y}{6} \\\\ 4 & <\\frac{6y}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can cancel the common factor $6$ from the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & <\\frac{6y}{6} \\\\ 4 & <\\frac{\\cancel{6}y}{\\cancel{6}} \\\\ 4 & <y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the inequality with the variable on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\ny>4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y>4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489283 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054770 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "281841fb-287e-597a-abb1-3917212e0dcb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a One-Step Inequality When Flipping Is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08e2c3c6-ae22-5a80-aebc-7813128a5a37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08e2c3c6-ae22-5a80-aebc-7813128a5a37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488492} :answer-field/id #uuid "25e54197-c5b1-5486-ba2f-8ba62d98a2d2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489041} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04704317-4fe6-5e5a-9496-2f63e3830ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04704317-4fe6-5e5a-9496-2f63e3830ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488481} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae7579b4-0642-5a3b-9317-adf97c57c0c7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489110}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eadfd460-afeb-5be8-ba9d-32eedcec4158" :question/math-academy-id "q-181139" :question/problem "The solution to the inequality $-2u>-1$ is $u${{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The variable $u$ is being *multiplied* by $-2.$ To isolate $u,$ we perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-2.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\nAlso, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2u\\,\\, & >\\,\\,-1 \\\\ \\frac{-2u}{-2}\\,\\, & <\\,\\,\\frac{-1}{-2} \\\\ \\frac{-2u}{-2}\\,\\, & <\\,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $-2$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-2u}{-2}\\,\\, & <\\,\\,\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-2}u}{\\cancel{-2}} & <\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ u & <\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $u<\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489193 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054771 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "200fc394-b299-5114-8f39-e6265f3c1166" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a One-Step Inequality With Fractions When Flipping Is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37fd20a8-7d5e-59b1-a20f-b74ee738720b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37fd20a8-7d5e-59b1-a20f-b74ee738720b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488585} :answer-field/id #uuid "9febe4e4-9bba-517f-959d-bd5f66e0861c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4a8742a-2daa-546c-b4d9-fbc8f9111dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4a8742a-2daa-546c-b4d9-fbc8f9111dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488832} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9f64c01-1af9-5569-9108-05d2c71dd293" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "24cf9a94-daed-5188-bbde-60124c7a3e18" :question/math-academy-id "q-181189" :question/problem "The solution to the inequality $-\\frac{y}{3}\\le 4$ is $y${{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The variable $y$ is being *divided* by $3.$ To isolate $y$ and remove the negative sign, we *multiply* by $-3.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{y}{3}\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,4 \\\\ (-3)\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{3})\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,(-3)\\cdot 4 \\\\ (-3)\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{3})\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince two negative numbers multiply to give a positive number, we first cancel the negatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{3})\\,\\, & \\ge -12 \\\\ (\\cancel{-}3)\\cdot (\\cancel{-}\\frac{y}{3}) & \\ge -12 \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{y}{3} & \\ge -12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $3$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot \\frac{y}{3} & \\ge -12 \\\\ \\frac{3y}{3} & \\ge -12 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{3}y}{\\cancel{3}} & \\ge -12 \\\\ y & \\ge -12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y\\ge -12.$"}]}
